-- 99: Northeast fishing rules (US plan step 4): New York, Connecticut, Vermont, New Hampshire
-- Checked 2026-10-21 on each state's own pages (links in source_url): NY DEC saltwater table (changed May 12, 2026) and freshwater statewide table
-- ("effective April 1, 2026"); CT DEEP species pages (saltwater: content updated April 2026; freshwater: December 2025 + trout 9 inch rule from Jan 1, 2026);
-- Vermont Fish & Wildlife guide on eRegulations (2026-27 guide, Table 1 updated Dec 16, 2025); New Hampshire Fish and Game haddock notice (Mar 31, 2026).
-- A state rule is a normal fish_rules row whose `regions` holds the 2-letter state code. Needs setup/94 first (its check allows these codes).
-- Where a rule changes by season or by water the app can only show one number, so the STRICTER one is the size/bag and the note has the rest.
-- NOT added (the state's own page was blocked or out of date when checked, so nothing could be read): Massachusetts (mass.gov blocked),
-- Rhode Island (dem.ri.gov blocked), Maine (maine.gov blocked), and every New Hampshire rule except haddock. Also not added: Connecticut cod/haddock
-- (the page says see the federal rules), New York and Vermont catfish (no statewide rule listed), Vermont pickerel (no rule listed).
-- The app says "We don't have a <State> rule for this fish yet" for those. Insert only; no delete / drop.

insert into fish_rules (species, match, regions, min_in, max_in, measure, one_over, bag, release_only, closed, open_only, note, source_url, verified_on, active) values
